---
source: crates/cli/tests/lint.rs
expression: out(&one)
---
sorted-keys
  languages:     json, yaml
  category:      style
  default level: off
  fix:           unsafe

The keys of an object are not in order (alphabetical by default). The keys that would have to move (the fewest) are reported and the first report carries the fix. Comments on lines of their own stay where they are.

Options:
  order (a list of strings, default []): Keys that come first, in this order; the rest follow in the configured order.
  direction (a string, default "asc"): `asc` or `desc`.
  compare (a string, default "ordinal"): `ordinal` (code points), `case_insensitive`, or `natural` (digit runs compare as numbers: `a2` before `a10`).
  ignored_keys (a list of strings, default []): Regular expressions; matching keys stay where they are and are not compared.
  min_keys (an integer, default 2): Mappings with fewer keys are not checked.
  blank_line_groups (a boolean, default false): Sort each run of entries between blank lines on its own.

Example:
  { "b": 1, "a": 2 }   // becomes { "a": 2, "b": 1 }
